[00:08.369]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[00:09.819]Where the balladeers play
[00:11.345]And the spirits never sleep
[00:14.162]Where the whispers call
[00:15.642]And the legends crawl
[00:17.058]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[00:19.508]...
[00:20.684]The night was still
[00:21.687]And the air was stale
[00:22.857]And the stench of ale ran high
[00:25.579]And it flowed from a pub across a cobblestone street
[00:28.616]Where a sailor was passing by
[00:31.822]Oh he drank his fill and he sang his song
[00:34.445]As the room began to sway
[00:37.206]Then he stumbled down the road to the waters edge
[00:40.182]Of a place called broken mast bay
[00:42.197]...
[00:42.840]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[00:44.581]Where the balladeers play
[00:46.017]And the spirits never sleep
[00:48.785]Where the whispers call
[00:50.272]And the legends crawl
[00:51.754]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[00:54.246]...
[00:55.092]With a dizzy head and a daring heart
[00:57.518]And a dingy on the shore
[01:00.162]In his drunken glee he put out to sea
[01:03.321]And he rowed to the mists of nore
[01:06.325]As he rowed along he could hear a song
[01:09.102]From a voice so pure and clear
[01:12.031]Then a selkie rose right beside his boat
[01:14.973]As her voice echoes in his ear
[01:17.400]...
[01:17.633]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[01:19.250]Where the balladeers play
[01:20.686]And the spirits never sleep
[01:23.432]Where the whispers call
[01:25.003]And the legends crawl
[01:26.547]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[01:28.811]...
[01:29.649]"come again?" said he "how can this be?"
[01:32.095]"have i had too much too drink?"
[01:35.121]"not at all" she sighed with a sparkle in her eyes
[01:38.165]"I'm as true as the ocean is deep"
[01:41.207]"why sail alone, my sailor bold, on this quiet moonlit night?"
[01:46.599]The sailor gawked as she whispered soft
[01:49.573]"please stay with me till light"
[01:51.723]...
[01:52.211]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[01:53.929]Where the balladeers play
[01:55.425]And the spirits never sleep
[01:58.113]Where the whispers call
[01:59.641]And the legends crawl
[02:01.178]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[02:03.583]...
[02:07.595]She shed a tear as he slurred his words
[02:10.362]Telling tales of life before
[02:13.435]How his friends were swallowed in the treacherous swells
[02:18.527]When they were claimed by the ocean floor
[02:21.219]...
[02:39.060]He wiped his eyes as the dawn advanced
[02:41.599]On a tired wakeless world
[02:44.333]Then she left a gift in his callous tent
[02:47.533]Was a pendant made of pearl
[02:50.674]"hold this close when the road feels long and the waves don't flow your way"
[02:55.883]" when you feel alone listen for my voice on the winds of broken mast bay"
[03:00.691]...
[03:01.492]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[03:03.016]Where the balladeers play
[03:04.597]And the spirits never sleep
[03:07.354]Where the whispers call
[03:09.012]And the legends crawl
[03:10.254]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[03:13.232]Ooh Broken Mast Bay
[03:14.670]Where the balladeers play
[03:16.224]And the spirits never sleep
[03:19.111]Where the whispers call
[03:20.559]And the legends crawl
[03:22.145]Through the veil of the ocean deep
[03:24.546]...
[03:29.709]The years sailed on and the selkies song
[03:32.369]Became a memory on the wind
[03:35.342]And the gift she gave found a shallow grave
[03:38.253]In a box where his memories lived
[03:41.629]Until one day in the village square
[03:44.092]He heard a voice that he once knew
[03:47.427]When he turned around he saw the sparkle in her eyes
[03:52.871]"old friend I've been waiting for you..."
